&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;DeepIntent is the leading healthcare marketing platform, purpose-built to help marketers plan, activate, and optimize data-driven campaigns with speed and precision. Trusted by the world’s top healthcare brands and their agencies, DeepIntent uniquely unites media, identity, and real-world clinical data to power privacy-safe, omnichannel marketing across every screen. Backed by patented technology and proven outcomes, DeepIntent’s platform delivers measurable audience quality and script lift at scale. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deepintent.com&quot;&gt;www.deepintent.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeepIntent is looking for a VP, Product Marketing to join our growing Marketing team. This role leads product marketing for DeepIntent’s platform and data products, owning positioning, messaging, launch, and the go-to-market motion that brings new capability to market. Reporting to the CMO and a member of the Marketing Leadership team, the VP, Product Marketing leads an established function and partners closely with Product, Sales, and Client Success to translate a sophisticated technology portfolio into a story pharma and agency buyers act on — advancing our mission to improve patient outcomes through better healthcare marketing technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an experienced product marketing leader who is equally comfortable with sophisticated technology and the realities of pharma commercialization — someone who can turn a complex product portfolio into clear positioning, packaging, and enablement, and who will raise the strategic bar of a function that is already in place&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Positioning &amp;amp; Messaging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the positioning, messaging, and proof points for DeepIntent’s product portfolio, ensuring the company’s innovation is effectively marketed and positioned externally, and with key internal go-to-market stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clear, differentiated product narrative in a competitive healthcare technology market that is provocative, compelling and engaging.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the product story holds up with pharma commercial, medical, and agency audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Launch &amp;amp; Go-to-Market&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end go-to-market for product releases — audience, narrative, packaging, launch plan, and success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product on roadmap sequencing and inform how offerings are packaged and priced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a repeatable launch process that scales with the product portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Buyer &amp;amp; Competitive Intelligence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain deep working knowledge of pharma commercialization buyers — brand, omnichannel, market access, medical, and data science.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run continuous competitive and market analysis, and turn it into decisions Product and Sales can act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the voice of the customer into roadmap, packaging, and pricing conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Enablement &amp;amp; Commercial Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across marketing to ensure the effective and successful positioning of DeepIntent innovation externally.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Equip Sales and Client Success with the demos, business cases, ROI frameworks, and objection handling they need to win.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Integrated Marketing to convert the product narrative into pipeline, and set KPIs that tie product marketing to revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support enterprise pursuits and partner motions across agencies, consultancies, and holding companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop DeepIntent’s product marketing team, elevating the function’s strategic role within Marketing and with Product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to the CMO, Product leadership, and the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of product marketing experience, including senior leadership of a product marketing function. Pharma and/or healthcare experience strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record marketing enterprise technology products — platform, software, or SaaS — to sophisticated business buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing products built on data science and machine learning, with the ability to translate technical capability into commercial value without overclaiming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with pharma commercialization: how brands launch, how HCP and patient engagement works, and how commercial, medical, and regulatory review shape what can be said.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success launching new products and sharpening a product narrative in a crowded, fast-moving market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to and through enterprise buyers in regulated industries, including partner and channel motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning packaging and pricing input for technology products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record building enablement programs that measurably shorten sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing a product marketing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional partner to Product, Sales, and Client Success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated with high energy and willingness to adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeepIntent is proud to offer a competitive compensation package inclusive of a base salary range of $275,000 - $310,000. The base salary range takes into consideration each candidate&#39;s skills, experience and qualifications. In addition, we offer an annualized bonus/commissions plan and competitive benefits as well as many other company offerings&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;We believe great work starts with great support. That’s why DeepIntent offers a competitive, holistic benefits package designed to empower you both professionally and personally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what you can expect when you join our team based in the US: Competitive base salary plus performance based bonus or commission, comprehensive medical, dental, and vision insurance, 401K match program, flexible PTO policy and paid holidays, remote friendly culture with flexible work options, career development and advanced education support, WFH and internet stipends, plus many more perks and benefits!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here’s what you can expect when you join our team based in India:&amp;nbsp;Competitive base salary plus performance based bonus, comprehensive medical insurance, and paid holidays. Hybrid-friendly culture with flexible work options, professional development reimbursement, WiFi reimbursement and health and wellness allowance plus many more perks and benefits!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here&#39;s what you can expect when you join our team based in Europe: Competitive base salary plus performance-based bonus, comprehensive medical insurance, and flexible PTO. Hybrid-friendly culture with flexible work options, professional development reimbursement, WiFi reimbursement, and parental leave plus many more perks and benefits!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DeepIntent is committed to bringing together individuals from different backgrounds and perspectives. We strive to create an inclusive environment where everyone can thrive, feel a sense of belonging, and do great work together.&amp;nbsp;DeepIntent is an Equal Opportunity Employer, providing equal employment and advancement opportunities to all individuals. We recruit, hire and promote into all job levels the most qualified applicants without regard to race, color, creed, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth and related medical conditions), parental status, age, disability, genetic information, citizenship status, veteran status, gender identity or expression, transgender status, sexual orientation, marital, family or partnership status, political affiliation or activities, military service, immigration status, or any other status protected under applicable federal, state and local laws. If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please let us know in advance.&amp;nbsp;DeepIntent’s commitment to providing equal employment opportunities extends to all aspects of employment, including job assignment, compensation, discipline and access to benefits and training.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CCPA Notice: If you are a California resident applying for a role at DeepIntent, we may collect personal information as part of the application process in accordance with the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA). To learn more about the categories of information we collect and your rights, please contact &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:PeopleOps@deepintent.com&quot;&gt;PeopleOps@deepintent.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see our full Applicant Privacy Notice.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;DeepIntent is the leading healthcare marketing platform, purpose-built to help marketers plan, activate, and optimize data-driven campaigns with speed and precision. Trusted by the world’s top healthcare brands and their agencies, DeepIntent uniquely unites media, identity, and real-world clinical data to power privacy-safe, omnichannel marketing across every screen. Backed by patented technology and proven outcomes, DeepIntent’s platform delivers measurable audience quality and script lift at scale. Learn more at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.deepintent.com&quot;&gt;www.deepintent.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Enterprise Sales will be responsible for cultivating high-value partnerships with pharmaceutical companies by integrating DeepIntent’s technology, data, and audience solutions into their commercial operations, marketing technology stacks, and customer engagement strategies. The Sr Director, Enterprise Sales has a deep understanding of how pharmaceutical companies leverage data, technology, and media to drive commercial success and a strong track record of developing JBPs that increase long-term revenue and integration depth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will work cross-functionally within pharmaceutical organizations, engaging with key teams responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing and Commercial Strategy – Driving digital transformation, omnichannel marketing execution, and audience engagement to optimize HCP and patient outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales and Commercial Operations – Overseeing field force effectiveness, sales enablement, and data-driven decision-making to improve brand performance and customer engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; Information Management – Managing commercial and real-world data strategy, including customer insights, identity resolution, and integration of external data sources into pharma’s analytics ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Experience and Digital Intelligence – Optimizing the use of technology to create personalized, data-driven experiences that enhance engagement with healthcare professionals and patients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technology and Innovation – Leading the integration of emerging tools such as AI, data workbenches, and programmatic solutions into the pharma ecosystem to enhance targeting, measurement, and attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Media Investment &amp;amp; Audience Optimization – Strategizing paid media and programmatic investments to ensure optimal reach, efficiency, and impact across digital channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop &amp;amp; Strengthen Pharma Partnerships – Drive meaningful, long-term strategic relationships with pharmaceutical clients, embedding DeepIntent’s technology and solutions into their business workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Joint Business Partnership Initiatives – Structure, negotiate, and execute JBPs that align DeepIntent’s media capabilities with pharma commercial priorities, driving deeper collaboration and investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate DeepIntent’s Solutions into Pharma Tech Stacks – Partner with clients to connect DeepIntent’s identity, audience, analytics, and activation solutions with their internal data ecosystems, CDPs, and measurement frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand Audience Connectivity &amp;amp; Activation – Work with pharma teams to optimize audience strategies, helping them reach HCPs and patients through more data-driven, AI-powered approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate Cross-Functionally – Serve as the bridge between Client Strategy, Product, Data Science, and Engineering to ensure that partnerships translate into impactful solutions and tangible business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Revenue Growth &amp;amp; Market Differentiation – Identify and execute commercial opportunities that strengthen DeepIntent’s position as a preferred pharma partner, expanding our role beyond media execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in AdTech, MarTech, and programmatic media, preferably with a strong focus on pharmaceutical commercial partnerships and data-driven marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
